<title>USA: LPC - Leading lenders to Latin American borrowers.</title>
<headline>LPC - Leading lenders to Latin American borrowers.</headline>
<text>
<p>NEW YORK, Feb 10 (LPC) - The following are providers of loans to Latin American borrowers during 1996, as compiled by Loan Pricing Corp.</p>
<p>This agent-only table awards credit for the full amount of a deal to each bank with an administrative agent, syndication agent, documentation agent or arranger title on that deal. Rank    Lender			  Volume		   Deals</p>
<p>1	 Chase Manhattan	   $5,841,891,967	     50</p>
<p>2	 BankAmerica		  5,542,000,000	     33</p>
<p>3	 Citicorp		     4,995,327,000	     31</p>
<p>4	 J.P. Morgan &amp; Co	   4,814,000,000	     24</p>
<p>5	 ABN AMRO Bank		3,064,300,000	     18</p>
<p>6	 Dresdner Bank		2,685,100,000	     14</p>
<p>7	 Barclays/BZW		 1,953,700,000	     15</p>
<p>8	 Santander Investment     1,820,500,000	     15</p>
<p>9	 ING Barings		  1,735,500,000	     15</p>
<p>10	Societe Generale	   1,636,000,000		9</p>
<p>11	Swiss Bank Corp	    1,544,000,000		6</p>
<p>12	UBS			    1,338,400,000		7</p>
<p>13	Industrial Bank of Japan   987,300,000		5</p>
<p>14	Bank of Boston		 952,234,000	     14</p>
<p>15	Westdeutsche Landesbank    860,500,000		7</p>
<p>((-- Meredith Coffey, LPC Editorial, 212 489-5455))</p>
